<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Ambiani</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.) · capital Samarobriva</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Belgic people of the Somme valley whose town Samarobriva, modern Amiens, hosted Caesar's council of Gaul in 54 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ambiani held the lower and middle Somme in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picardy">Picardy</a>. Caesar records that they promised ten thousand warriors to the Belgic league of 57 BCE and surrendered after the league broke up.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their oppidum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiens">Samarobriva</a>, the bridge on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somme-river">Samara</a> or Somme, controlled a key crossing. They struck abundant gold coins, some of the earliest in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Caesar held an assembly of the Gallic peoples at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiens">Samarobriva</a> in 54 BCE and wintered there. The Ambiani sent men to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alesia">Alesia</a> in 52 BCE and fought again in 51 BCE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> Samarobriva became a major city, later Ambianum, the origin of Amiens.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ambiani.jpg" alt="Ambiani" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ambiani_hemi_stater_Gallica_celtiques_688_avers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Samarobriva</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=ambiani" aria-label="Ambiani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4733 441 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ambiani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5053 697L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5053 697h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5053 697h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Samarobriva. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=ambiani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

